{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qt7de2hbsp54nnk4yxgzdiwp5ttobuynnlufacpl3megtqzxbfiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found a real harness bug (`temp_key` is uninitialized by `stbds_make_hash_index`, so dereferencing it faults). Let me fix the snapshot to be deref-free and compare `temp_key` relationally:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4603,"cache_read_input_tokens":149307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4603,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e281560-6e2e-4739-ae65-99f125918909","uuid":"8571ba47-3f36-4831-a6a7-547e0f041728","timestamp":"2026-08-27T18:12:42.668Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qt7de2hbsp54nnk4yxgzdiwp5ttobuynnlufacpl3megtqzxbfiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01XLAiTEU596achKhoqw2BaA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/common/mod.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\n\n# 1) drop temp_key deref from TableSnap\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"pub struct TableSnap {\n    pub temp_key: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n    pub slot_count: usize,\"\"\",\"\"\"pub struct TableSnap {\n    /// NOTE: `stbds_hash_index::temp_key` is deliberately **absent**.\n    /// `stbds_make_hash_index` never initialises it (not even when rehashing\n    /// from an old table), so it holds `realloc` garbage until the first\n    /// `hmput_key` in a pointer-key mode writes it. Dereferencing it from the\n    /// harness would fault. It is instead compared *relationally* in\n    /// `MapPair::put` (see `temp_key_rel`), which is exactly what the\n    /// `stbds_shputs` macro observes.\n    pub slot_count: usize,\"\"\")\n\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"    TableSnap {\n        temp_key: read_cstr(t.temp_key),\n        slot_count: t.slot_count,\"\"\",\"\"\"    TableSnap {\n        slot_count: t.slot_count,\"\"\")\n\n# 2) rework put()'s temp_key check\nold = \"\"\"            let ic = map_temp(tc, self.elemsize);\n            let ir = map_temp(tr, self.elemsize);\n            assert_same(\"hmput_key temp index\", &ic, &ir);\n            let kc = read_cstr(map_temp_key(tc, self.elemsize));\n            let kr = read_cstr(map_temp_key(tr, self.elemsize));\n            assert_same(\"hmput_key temp_key content\", &kc, &kr);\n            let p = value.to_le_bytes();\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"            let ic = map_temp(tc, self.elemsize);\n            let ir = map_temp(tr, self.elemsize);\n            assert_same(\"hmput_key temp index\", &ic, &ir);\n            self.check_temp_key(key, ic);\n            let p = value.to_le_bytes();\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# 3) add check_temp_key + stores_ptr flag\nold = \"\"\"    /// bytes at element offset 0 that the *library* owns (8 for a stored\n    /// `char *`, `keysize` for a raw binary/memcpy key)\n    pub skip: usize,\n    pub kind: KeyKind,\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    /// bytes at element offset 0 that the *library* owns (8 for a stored\n    /// `char *`, `keysize` for a raw binary/memcpy key)\n    pub skip: usize,\n    /// true when `table->string.mode` is one of SH_DEFAULT/STRDUP/ARENA, i.e.\n    /// element offset 0 holds a `char *` and `temp_key` is maintained.\n    pub stores_ptr: bool,\n    pub sh: c_int,\n    pub kind: KeyKind,\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\n\nold = \"\"\"        MapPair {\n            c,\n            rs,\n            elemsize,\n            keysize,\n            mode,\n            skip,\n            kind,\n            capi,\n            rapi,\n        }\n    }\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"        MapPair {\n            c,\n            rs,\n            elemsize,\n            keysize,\n            mode,\n            skip,\n            stores_ptr,\n            sh,\n            kind,\n            capi,\n            rapi,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// `stbds_temp_key` is what `stbds_shputs` reads immediately after a put.\n    /// It is compared without ever dereferencing garbage:\n    ///\n    /// * SH_DEFAULT -- must be *exactly* the caller's key pointer (both\n    ///   libraries were handed the same pointer, so this is byte-exact);\n    /// * SH_STRDUP / SH_ARENA -- the address differs between libraries, so we\n    ///   compare (a) whether it aliases the element's stored key pointer and\n    ///   (b) the string content when it does;\n    /// * otherwise (`default:` branch) -- the C never writes it, so nothing is\n    ///   compared.\n    #[track_caller]\n    fn check_temp_key(&self, key: *mut c_void, idx: isize) {\n        if !self.stores_ptr || self.elemsize < 8 {\n            return;\n        }\n        unsafe {\n            let tkc = map_temp_key(self.c, self.elemsize);\n            let tkr = map_temp_key(self.rs, self.elemsize);\n            let ekc = *((self.c as *const u8).offset(idx * self.elemsize as isize)\n                as *const *mut c_char);\n            let ekr = *((self.rs as *const u8).offset(idx * self.elemsize as isize)\n                as *const *mut c_char);\n            if self.sh == SH_DEFAULT {\n                assert_same(\n                    \"SH_DEFAULT temp_key == caller key\",\n                    &(tkc as usize == key as usize),\n                    &(tkr as usize == key as usize),\n                );\n                assert_same(\n                    \"SH_DEFAULT elem key == caller key\",\n                    &(ekc as usize == key as usize),\n                    &(ekr as usize == key as usize),\n                );\n                return;\n            }\n            let alias_c = tkc as usize == ekc as usize;\n            let alias_r = tkr as usize == ekr as usize;\n            assert_same(\"temp_key aliases element key\", &alias_c, &alias_r);\n            if alias_c {\n                assert_same(\n                    \"temp_key content\",\n                    &read_cstr(tkc),\n                    &read_cstr(tkr),\n                );\n            }\n        }\n    }\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY\ncargo check --offline --tests 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Make temp_key comparison deref-free"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4603,"cache_read_input_tokens":149307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4603,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e281560-6e2e-4739-ae65-99f125918909","uuid":"9a75cafc-e2ef-42b4-aef2-d4f5d07ca3e5","timestamp":"2026-08-27T18:13:01.951Z"}
